.TH LOGGER 2 "2026-05-02" "4.3" "Logger Library Manual"
.SH NAME
logger \- full API reference for the Logger library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "logger.h"
.SH DESCRIPTION
This page documents all logging functions, helper utilities and sink/FFI helpers.
For introduction and lifecycle functions see
.BR logger (1).
For internals and architecture see
.BR logger (3).
.SH LOGGING FUNCTIONS
Log functions come in two flavours:
.IP \(bu 4
.B Implicit instance
\(em operate on the active instance set by
.BR lg_set_active_instance .
.IP \(bu 4
.B Explicit instance
(\fBi\fR suffix) \(em take a
.I Logger*
as the first argument. Passing
.B NULL
falls back to the active instance.
.PP
Each flavour also has an
.B f
(formatted/pre-formatted) variant that takes a plain
.B const char*
and is always available regardless of compiler version or
.BR LOGGER_BUILD .
The variadic variants disappear when
.B LOGGER_BUILD
is defined.
.SS Low-level producers
.TP
.BR "int lg_log_" "(Logger *inst, LgLogLevel level, const char *msg, size_t msglen)"
Core producer. Pushes a pre-formatted message directly into the ring buffer.
Not recommended for direct use; prefer the higher-level functions below.
.TP
.BR "int lg_vlog_" "(Logger *inst, LgLogLevel level, const char *fmt, va_list ap)"
Applies printf-style formatting via
.I ap
then calls
.BR lg_log_ .
Use this when forwarding variadic arguments from your own functions.
.SS Variadic functions (implicit instance)
.TP
.BR "int lg_log" "(LgLogLevel level, const char *fmt, ...)"
Log with explicit level, implicit instance.
.TP
.BR "int lg_info" "(const char *fmt, ...)"
.TQ
.BR "int lg_warn" "(const char *fmt, ...)"
.TQ
.BR "int lg_error" "(const char *fmt, ...)"
.TQ
.BR "int lg_custom" "(const char *fmt, ...)"
Convenience wrappers for each log level with implicit instance.
.SS Variadic functions (explicit instance)
.TP
.BR "int lg_logi" "(Logger *inst, LgLogLevel level, const char *fmt, ...)"
Log with explicit level and explicit instance.
.TP
.BR "int lg_infoi" "(Logger *inst, const char *fmt, ...)"
.TQ
.BR "int lg_warni" "(Logger *inst, const char *fmt, ...)"
.TQ
.BR "int lg_errori" "(Logger *inst, const char *fmt, ...)"
.TQ
.BR "int lg_customi" "(Logger *inst, const char *fmt, ...)"
Convenience wrappers with explicit instance.
.SS Pre-formatted functions, implicit instance (f prefix, always available)
.TP
.BR "int lg_flog" "(LgLogLevel level, const char *msg)"
.TP
.BR "int lg_finfo" "(const char *msg)"
.TQ
.BR "int lg_fwarn" "(const char *msg)"
.TQ
.BR "int lg_ferror" "(const char *msg)"
.TQ
.BR "int lg_fcustom" "(const char *msg)"
.SS Pre-formatted functions, explicit instance (fi suffix, always available)
.TP
.BR "int lg_flogi" "(Logger *inst, LgLogLevel level, const char *msg)"
.TP
.BR "int lg_finfoi" "(Logger *inst, const char *msg)"
.TQ
.BR "int lg_fwarni" "(Logger *inst, const char *msg)"
.TQ
.BR "int lg_ferrori" "(Logger *inst, const char *msg)"
.TQ
.BR "int lg_fcustomi" "(Logger *inst, const char *msg)"
.SH HELPER FUNCTIONS
.TP
.BR "const char* lg_lvl_to_str" "(LgLogLevel level)"
Converts a
.I LgLogLevel
enum value to a human-readable C string
.RB ( \(dqINFO\(dq ", " \(dqERROR\(dq ", " \(dqWARNING\(dq ", " \(dqCUSTOM\(dq ).
.TP
.BR "int lg_get_time_str" "(Logger *inst, char *buf)"
Writes the current timestamp into
.I buf
in the format
.B YYYY.MM.DD-HH.MM.SS.mmm
(including the NUL terminator).
.I buf
must be at least
.B LOGGER_TIME_STR_SIZE
(24) bytes.
Timestamp is evaluated at the consumer (writer) thread, not at call time.
.TP
.BR "void lg_str_format_into" "(LgString *s, const char *fmt, ...)"
printf-style formatter that writes into an
.I LgString
struct. Guarantees a trailing newline and NUL terminator.
Useful inside custom formatter callbacks.
.TP
.BR "void lg_str_write_into" "(LgString *s, const char *str)"
Copies a NUL-terminated string into an
.I LgString
struct.
.TP
.BR "int lg_is_alive" "(const Logger *instance)"
Returns 1 if the instance is running. Pass NULL to check the active instance.
.SH CUSTOM FORMATTER
Assign a
.B log_formatter_t
to
.I LoggerConfig.logFormatter
to override the default layout
.RB ( "time_str [level] msg" ).
.PP
Prototype:
.nf
typedef int (*log_formatter_t)(
    const char  *time_str,
    LgLogLevel   level,
    const char  *msg,
    uint32_t     needed,
    LgMsgPack    out
);
.fi
.PP
.I needed
is a bitmask of
.B LgOutType
flags indicating which sink types are active.
Use
.B LOGGER_CONTAINS_FLAG(needed, LG_OUT_TTY)
etc. to guard each output.
Write into the appropriate
.B LgString
inside
.I out
using
.BR lg_str_format_into .
Always append
.B \\n
at the end. Return 1 on success.
.PP
Example:
.nf
int myFormatter(const char *time_str, LgLogLevel level,
                const char *msg, uint32_t needed, LgMsgPack pack) {
    const char *lvl = lg_lvl_to_str(level);
    if (LOGGER_CONTAINS_FLAG(needed, LG_OUT_TTY))
        lg_str_format_into(&pack[LG_OUT_TTY],
                           "%s/%s: %s\\n", time_str, lvl, msg);
    if (LOGGER_CONTAINS_FLAG(needed, LG_OUT_FILE))
        lg_str_format_into(&pack[LG_OUT_FILE],
                           "%s/%s: %s\\n", time_str, lvl, msg);
    return 1;
}
.fi
.SH FFI / FILE HELPERS
In FFI contexts, do not use the host language's file primitives.
Use the following wrappers instead to avoid double-free and GC conflicts.
.TP
.BR "FILE* lg_get_stdout" "(void)"
Returns
.BR stdout .
.TP
.BR "FILE* lg_get_stderr" "(void)"
Returns
.BR stderr .
.TP
.BR "FILE* lg_fopen" "(const char *path)"
Opens
.I path
in
.B wb
mode as required by the library's
.BR fwrite -based
payload processor.
.SH ADDING CUSTOM LOG LEVELS
Add a new entry to the
.B LG_LOG_LEVELS
X-macro and, if using
.IR loggerstream.hpp ,
define the corresponding stream macro there. No other changes are required.
